---
title: "Figure 4 — Sequence State Machine: the recon-add-drain kill chain"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> S0_IDLE

    S0_IDLE --> S1_BALANCE : get_balance\n(ALLOW per-call)
    note left of S0_IDLE
        State keyed on (session_id, resource_principal).
        Advances only on a permitted, successful call.
        Nothing the agent does resets state (D12);
        idle expiry/session end clears only live state;
        per-chain cap evictions are logged.
        New sessions replay 24h of principal history (D15);
        named binding digests are reconstructible.
    end note

    S1_BALANCE --> S2_PAYEES : list_payees\n(ALLOW per-call)
    S2_PAYEES --> S3_PAYEE_ADDED : add_payee(p) succeeds\n(ALLOW per-call)\nbind payee digest = H(p)

    S3_PAYEE_ADDED --> S4_BLOCKED : transfer_funds(H(to) = H(p))\nBLOCKING -> DENY\nrule_id seq.recon_add_drain.terminal
    S3_PAYEE_ADDED --> S3_PAYEE_ADDED : transfer_funds(H(to) != H(p))\nsequence -> None; ordinary D5 GATE\npreserve S3 (D16)
    note right of S3_PAYEE_ADDED
        False-block guard:
        a bare add_payee -> transfer_funds
        with no recon prefix never reaches S3.
        A transfer to a different/pre-existing payee
        returns None from sequence; normal D5 GATE applies,
        and operator approval lets it pass.
    end note

    S1_BALANCE --> S1_BALANCE : benign call\n(interleaving ignored)
    S2_PAYEES --> S2_PAYEES : benign call\n(interleaving ignored)
    S3_PAYEE_ADDED --> S3_PAYEE_ADDED : successful duplicate add_payee\n(idempotent digest re-bind)

    S1_BALANCE --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)
    S2_PAYEES --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)
    S3_PAYEE_ADDED --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)

    S4_BLOCKED --> [*] : DENY recorded in audit log\n(transfer never executed)
